4. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2475 — `.edit` reads the editor's file back with an uncapped `read_to_string`, and src/repl/mod.rs:2595 hands it straight to `execute_code`/`run_code` with no `exceeds_block_limits` check, so the session's own 500-line/64 KiB block policy (src/repl/mod.rs:50-55, enforced on the typed path at :1133 and :1188) does not apply to this path at all — a runaway or merely large `$EDITOR` result is read entirely into memory and parsed; the REPORT.md:198 `resource_limit` row claims this area is "covered" — cap `edited` with the same `exceeds_block_limits` check before reading or running, and add a test on both sides of the cap.
5. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2458 — `self.write_scratch_file(&scratch)?` returns before the `remove_dir_all` at src/repl/mod.rs:2492, and src/repl/mod.rs:2520's `Self::lock_down_dir(&dir)?` does the same, so the two failure paths the comment at :2460-2463 explicitly promises are covered ("every path out of here takes the directory with it") both leak the new `redblue-edit-<pid>-<n>/` directory into `std::env::temp_dir()` — `edge_a_failed_edit_leaves_no_copy_of_the_buffer_behind` (src/repl/mod.rs:6633) pins a property the code does not have, since it only exercises spawn/exit failures — make the directory removal a scope guard (or fold the write into the same closure) and add a test that forces a write/lock failure.
